WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.884 --> 00:00:18.848
The old lady at the post office said to Bobbie, Phyllis, and Peter, "You're good little children.

2
00:00:20.009 --> 00:00:21.749
Here's a pram I'm not using.

3
00:00:21.769 --> 00:00:27.151
I bought it for my daughter's first baby, but he died at six months old.

4
00:00:28.611 --> 00:00:29.331
I'd like Mrs.

5
00:00:29.391 --> 00:00:32.232
Perks to have the pram for her baby," she said.

6
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:38.043
Phyllis hugged the old lady and said, "Oh, Perks will be pleased!"

7
00:00:39.324 --> 00:00:42.486
They packed all the gifts into the pram and took it to Perks' house.

8
00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:45.448
The garden was very tidy.

9
00:00:46.549 --> 00:00:48.511
A jug of daisies sat on the windowsill.

10
00:00:49.471 --> 00:00:50.672
Bobbie knocked on the door.

11
00:00:51.793 --> 00:00:52.934
Mrs. Perks came out.

12
00:00:53.974 --> 00:00:55.555
"We've got some presents for Mr.

13
00:00:55.595 --> 00:00:57.437
Perks' birthday," said Peter.

14
00:00:58.798 --> 00:01:01.039
As they unpacked the presents, Mrs.

15
00:01:01.139 --> 00:01:02.000
Perks gasped.

16
00:01:03.301 --> 00:01:06.203
She surprised everyone by suddenly bursting into tears.

17
00:01:06.223 --> 00:01:09.686
"Oh don't!"

18
00:01:10.187 --> 00:01:10.887
said the children.

19
00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:14.270
Peter said impatiently, "What's the matter?"

20
00:01:15.591 --> 00:01:16.932
Mrs. Perks only sobbed.

21
00:01:17.713 --> 00:01:20.576
The Perks children stood at the door, looking uncomfortable.

22
00:01:22.297 --> 00:01:23.658
There was an awkward silence.

23
00:01:24.979 --> 00:01:26.501
Phyllis and Bobbie patted Mrs.

24
00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:27.401
Perks on the back.

25
00:01:28.623 --> 00:01:33.962
She stopped crying and said, "Perks has never had a birthday like this, not even when he was

26
00:01:34.043 --> 00:01:37.105
little. You children are very kind."

27
00:01:38.886 --> 00:01:41.087
Mrs. Perks put the buns and berries on plates.

28
00:01:42.288 --> 00:01:46.531
"Let's hide in the laundry, then come in and surprise Perks," whispered Bobbie.

29
00:01:47.692 --> 00:01:51.274
They quickly ran into the laundry, but there wasn't time to close the door.

30
00:01:53.075 --> 00:01:56.838
They had to push the young Perks children in front of them and all squeeze in together.

31
00:01:56.858 --> 00:02:00.240
"Hello!" Perks called out.

32
00:02:01.448 --> 00:02:02.308
"Isn't this pretty?

33
00:02:03.449 --> 00:02:05.509
It's your birthday tea," said Mrs.

34
00:02:05.609 --> 00:02:08.350
Perks. There was the sound of a kiss.

35
00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:12.531
"But what's that pram doing here?"

36
00:02:12.971 --> 00:02:13.511
said Perks.

37
00:02:13.531 --> 00:02:16.092
"What are all these things?

38
00:02:17.072 --> 00:02:19.673
Where did you get Mrs.

39
00:02:19.753 --> 00:02:20.853
Perks mumbled something.

40
00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:23.794
"I don't care," Perks said angrily.

41
00:02:23.814 --> 00:02:26.895
"We've been fine all these years.

42
00:02:28.095 --> 00:02:30.516
I'm not going to accept charity now!"

43
00:02:32.496 --> 00:02:33.737
"Shh!" said Mrs.

44
00:02:33.797 --> 00:02:37.560
Perks. "The children can hear everything you say!"

45
00:02:37.581 --> 00:02:41.304
"Good! I've got more to say to them!"

46
00:02:41.644 --> 00:02:42.164
he shouted.

47
00:02:43.165 --> 00:02:43.626
"Come out!

48
00:02:44.606 --> 00:02:45.968
Tell me why you did this!

49
00:02:46.988 --> 00:02:48.950
Did I say I needed anything?

50
00:02:49.951 --> 00:02:51.953
Why am I receiving this charity?"

51
00:02:53.174 --> 00:02:55.496
Perks sat down heavily in a chair and frowned.

52
00:02:56.837 --> 00:03:00.380
"Oh," said Phyllis, "I thought you'd be pleased.

53
00:03:01.572 --> 00:03:05.053
I'll never try to be kind again, I promise."

54
00:03:06.313 --> 00:03:07.434
She burst into tears.

55
00:03:07.454 --> 00:03:11.475
"We didn't mean to make you angry," Peter said.

56
00:03:11.495 --> 00:03:16.516
"It's not what you mean, it's what you do," said Perks.

57
00:03:16.536 --> 00:03:19.837
"But the presents are not all from us.

58
00:03:21.038 --> 00:03:23.258
They're from people in the village," Bobbie said.

59
00:03:23.278 --> 00:03:25.579
"And who asked for them?"

60
00:03:25.979 --> 00:03:26.499
said Perks.

61
00:03:26.519 --> 00:03:29.460
"We did," said Phyllis.

62
00:03:30.748 --> 00:03:35.192
"So you've told all the neighbors that we're poor and need charity?"

63
00:03:35.572 --> 00:03:36.133
asked Perks.

64
00:03:36.153 --> 00:03:41.557
"Well, you can just take the pram and the gifts and go home."

65
00:03:42.658 --> 00:03:45.521
He turned his chair around so that his back faced the children.

66
00:03:46.622 --> 00:03:47.883
Then suddenly Bobbie spoke.

67
00:03:47.903 --> 00:03:51.926
"The people in the village wanted to give you birthday presents."

68
00:03:53.647 --> 00:03:56.430
Perks slowly turned his chair around to face the children.

69
00:03:57.571 --> 00:03:58.812
He seemed a little less angry.

70
00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:01.661
Bobbie kept talking in a quiet voice.

71
00:04:02.761 --> 00:04:05.822
"The doctor said, 'I'm pleased to give something to Perks.

72
00:04:06.962 --> 00:04:08.282
He always pays his bills.'"

73
00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:14.524
Now Bobbie continued in a louder voice, "And the grocer said, 'Perks works hard.'

74
00:04:15.624 --> 00:04:21.286
And the lady at the post office said that you always—" "Stop," said Perks suddenly.

75
00:04:21.306 --> 00:04:24.407
"I take back every word.

76
00:04:25.507 --> 00:04:26.687
I didn't understand.

77
00:04:28.088 --> 00:04:33.637
I am pleased not just with the presents, but with the kind thoughts of our neighbors.

78
00:04:34.738 --> 00:04:37.180
They're the best presents of all, aren't they, Nell?"

79
00:04:38.201 --> 00:04:38.962
His wife nodded.

80
00:04:39.923 --> 00:04:40.984
Perks looked at the children.

81
00:04:41.004 --> 00:04:42.826
"You'll stay for tea?"

82
00:04:43.427 --> 00:04:45.369
"Yes, please!"

83
00:04:45.509 --> 00:04:45.889
they said.
